ces. It operates through two segments, U.S. Domestic Package and International Package. The U.S. Domestic Package segment offers time-definite delivery services for express letters, documents, packages and palletized freight through air and ground services. The International Package segment provides small package operations in Europe, the Middle East and Africa, Canada and Latin America, and Asia. The company offers a range of guaranteed day- and time-definite international transportation services; day-definite services; cross-border ground package delivery; contract-only, e-commerce solutions for non-urgent, and cross-border shipments; and international service for urgent and palletized shipments. It also provides international air and ocean freight forwarding, contract logistics, customs brokerage and insurance, mail services, healthcare logistics, distribution, and post-sales services. United Parcel Service, Inc. was founded in 1907 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Carol B. Tome | CEO & Director | Age 68 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 460K people. Revenue per employee of $193K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $159 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 21\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["United Parcel Service, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $95.7B market cap on $88.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $4.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.7\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 27% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","26 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"UPS or Comcast: I Can Only Pick One Dividend Stock for the Next 10 Years. Here\u2019s Mine","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ups-comcast-only-pick-one-144809253.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794581289.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"UPS Stock And Other Trade Compliance Winners From Mexico Tariff Risk","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nasdaq-chrw/ch-robinson-worldwide/news/ups-stock-and-other-trade-compliance-winners-from-mexico-tar","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794529462.486,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["regulatory"]},{"title":"A $400,000 Portfolio in UPS, Enterprise Products and Pfizer Pays $23,577 a Year in Dividends. Here\u2019s What Happens if One Cuts","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/400-000-portfolio-ups-enterprise-182033923.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794507633.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"USPS to add 11% permanent fuel surcharge along with parcel rate hike","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/articles/usps-add-11-permanent-fuel-190038392.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794596438.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.38,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"John Rogers's Top Q3 2026 Move: Qualcomm Inc at a 0.91% Portfolio Impact","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/john-rogerss-top-q3-2026-140037154.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794578437.0,"o